{
  "kanji": "器",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 器\ntitle: vessel; instrument\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 15\nradical: 口\nradicalNumber: 30\nonyomi: [キ]\nkunyomi: [うつわ]\nquizOnyomi: [キ]\nquizKunyomi: []\ndistractors: [品, 喜, 奇]\nquiz_exclusions: [缶, 皿, 瓶, 容, 具, 機, 械, 能, 才]\n---\n\n# 器 — vessel; instrument\n\n**Strokes:** 15 · **Key (radical):** 口 (no. 30), at the top left · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n器 is a container or a tool, and by extension a bodily organ or a person's capacity. [容器](../words/容器.md) ようき is a container, [食器](../words/食器.md) しょっき is tableware, [楽器](../words/楽器.md) がっき is a musical instrument, [武器](../words/武器.md) ぶき is a weapon, [器具](../words/器具.md) きぐ is a utensil or tool, [受話器](../words/受話器.md) じゅわき is a telephone receiver, and [器用](../words/器用.md) きよう is being dexterous or skillful.\n\nThe Daijisen character entry gives three senses: a container, or a tool made in a set shape, as in 楽器 and 食器; a part of a living body with a particular function and form, as in 器官 きかん, \"organ,\" and 臓器 ぞうき, \"internal organs; viscera\"; and a person's ability or talent, as in 器用 and 器量 きりょう, \"ability; capability; capacity.\" JMdict gives the standalone word 器 うつわ as \"bowl; vessel; container\" and \"ability; capacity; calibre,\" and 大器 たいき as \"large container\" and \"person of great talent.\"\n\nThe official Joyo table also prints an older form of 器 in round brackets, with a dot in its centre like 犬; this card teaches the standard form, whose centre is plain 大.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** find four [口](口.md), \"mouth,\" in the corners around a centre shape that is [大](大.md), \"big, large,\" with no dot. Imagine four mouths crowded around one big serving bowl, and remember 器 as a bowl or vessel. This is a memory aid only: it makes no claim that 口 or 大 contributes meaning or sound. Historical formation is not established here.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キ | on | [容器](../words/容器.md) ようき — container; receptacle; [食器](../words/食器.md) しょっき — tableware; dishes; [楽器](../words/楽器.md) がっき — musical instrument; [武器](../words/武器.md) ぶき — weapon; asset; [器具](../words/器具.md) きぐ — utensil; tool; apparatus; [受話器](../words/受話器.md) じゅわき — telephone receiver; handset; [器用](../words/器用.md) きよう — dexterous; skillful |\n| うつわ | kun | 器 うつわ - bowl; vessel; container; ability; capacity; not selected for questions here |\n\nIn 容器, 容 supplies ヨウ. In 食器, 食 supplies ショク, shortened to しょっ before キ. In 楽器, 楽 supplies ガク, shortened to がっ. In 武器, 武 supplies ブ. In 器具, 具 supplies グ and 器 comes first. In 受話器, 受 supplies ジュ and 話 supplies ワ. In 器用, 用 supplies ヨウ. The official Joyo table, the list of standard-use readings, shows キ and うつわ for 器. Practice selects キ, which has linked word articles; うつわ is the standalone word 器, which has no linked article yet, so no kun reading is selected for questions.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [容器](../words/容器.md) ようき — container; receptacle\n- [食器](../words/食器.md) しょっき — tableware; dishes\n- [楽器](../words/楽器.md) がっき — musical instrument\n- [武器](../words/武器.md) ぶき — weapon; asset\n- [器具](../words/器具.md) きぐ — utensil; tool; apparatus\n- [受話器](../words/受話器.md) じゅわき — telephone receiver; handset\n- [器用](../words/器用.md) きよう — dexterous; skillful\n\n## Notes\n\n- The other kanji in the common words are [容](容.md), \"contain; appearance,\" [食](食.md), \"eat, food,\" [楽](楽.md), \"music, enjoyment, ease,\" [武](武.md), \"military; warrior,\" [具](具.md), \"tools; ingredients,\" [受](受.md), \"receive; undergo,\" [話](話.md), \"talk, speak,\" and [用](用.md), \"use, purpose.\"\n- [品](品.md), \"goods, refinement,\" stacks three 口 and looks like part of 器, but it has no centre shape and no fourth 口. [喜](喜.md), \"rejoice,\" and [奇](奇.md), \"strange; extraordinary,\" also read キ but do not mean vessel or instrument.\n- [缶](缶.md), \"tin can; container,\" [皿](皿.md), \"dish; plate,\" [瓶](瓶.md), \"bottle; jar,\" and [容](容.md), \"contain; appearance,\" each overlap the \"container\" or \"vessel\" sense of 器. [具](具.md), \"tools; ingredients,\" overlaps its \"tool\" sense, and [機](機.md), \"mechanism; opportunity,\" and [械](械.md), \"machine; fetter,\" overlap its \"instrument\" sense. [能](能.md), \"ability; capacity,\" and [才](才.md), \"talent,\" overlap the \"ability\" sense. All of them are kept out of this card's quiz options. Do not treat \"vessel,\" \"tool\" or \"ability\" as exclusive to any one character.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-11-02 snapshot. Word identities and spelling restrictions: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1218880, 1218920, 1218960, 1545370, 1207340, 1498460, 1358430, 1330090, 1218910, 1403480, 1218980 and 1661020. Character reading and compounds: [Digital Daijisen, 器](https://www.weblio.jp/content/器).\n\nUsage evidence: [Official Joyo kanji table (2010), PDF p. 33](https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/pdf/joyokanjihyo_20101130.pdf#page=33).\n",
